<title>MEXICO: FORECAST-Mexico 28-day Cetes seen at 22.84 pct.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Mexico 28-day Cetes seen at 22.84 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Interest rates on Mexico's bellwether 28-day Cetes, or T-bills, are seen falling 22 basis points to 22.84 percent, and rates are expected to decline in longer terms too, according to a Reuters survey of 10 Cetes dealers.</p>
<p>Here is a table comparing last week's primary rates versus expectations for this week's auction and the expected change in basis points.</p>
<p>    TERM	LAST WEEK    THIS WEEK'S SURVEY   CHANGE</p>
<p>    28-DAY     23.06	    22.84		   - 22 bps</p>
<p>    91-DAY     25.63	    25.08		   - 55 bps</p>
<p>    182-DAY    27.33	    26.49		   - 84 bps</p>
<p>    1-YEAR     27.39	    26.93		   - 46 bps</p>
<p>The results will be released by Banco de Mexico at 1830 EDT.</p>
<p>--Mexico City newsroom 525 7289559</p>
</text>
